ham Drug (U.S.)] Cunningham Drug was a drugstore chain based in Detroit, Michigan.  Founded in October 1889 by Andrew Cunningham, the chain operated primarily within the state of Michigan, and was once the largest drugstore chain in the state.  Its Michigan locations were closed and reopened in 1982 as Apex Drug, and were later sold to Perry Drug Stores.  The last stores remained open in Florida until 1991, when they were sold to Walgreens.]\n\n[[Rexall] Rexall is a chain of American drugstores, and the name of their store-branded products.  The stores, having roots in the federation of United Drug Stores starting in 1903, licensed the Rexall brand name to as many as 12,000 drug stores across the United States from 1920 to 1977.  (The \"Rex\" in the name came from the common Rx abbreviation for medical prescriptions.)]\n\nQuestion: Which state does the drug stores, of which the CEO is Warren Bryant, are located?","terminal_format_issue":"Format Agent is not selected as the Output Agent","topology_statistics":{"agent_count":0,"component_count":0,"directed_edge_count":0,"fan_in_agent_ids":[],"fan_out_agent_ids":[],"max_depth":0,"max_width":0,"output_agent_id":null,"quotient_directed_edge_count":0,"reciprocal_pair_count":0,"relation_count":0,"root_agent_ids":[],"root_component_count":0,"sink_agent_ids":[],"sink_component_count":0,"structural_depth":0,"topology_family":"empty","topology_motifs":[]}}","role":"user"},{"content":"{
